  "why": "The statement is the two-sided Noetherian form. Herstein 1965 and Jategaonkar 1968 are one-sided counterexamples (the field still calls the two-sided form open), so they are variants, not refutations. The fully bounded, PI, Krull-dimension-one, second-layer, down-up and left-Noetherian-right-distributive results each settle a class of two-sided Noetherian rings, so they are cases, all journal-published and pre-2024. Tuganbaev's hypotheses are weaker on Noetherianity but plus distributivity; its conclusion covers two-sided Noetherian right distributive rings, so case. Brown–Lenagan (one-sided, conclusion intersected with a central subring), Krause (redefined transfinite powers), and the module/endomorphism-ring results are variants. The only post-snapshot items (Shin, Cimprič–Schötz, the Jacobian-conjecture namesake) concern different questions; the Alpöge AI claim is about the Jacobian conjecture and earns no AI role here.",
